`paginate_items(items, page_size)` accepts a list or tuple and returns a tuple of tuple pages, preserving item order. Every page except possibly the last contains exactly `page_size` items. Empty input returns `()`, and an exact multiple must not produce a trailing empty page. `page_size` must be a positive integer and must not be Boolean; invalid sizes raise `TypeError` or `ValueError`. Invalid `items` raises `TypeError`. Items are deeply copied so mutation of nested input values or returned values cannot cross the API boundary. The input container is not mutated.

